To allocate multiple stacks using the same method, we would need to define a separate memory region for each thread’s stack. Starting from MSP_init_val, we would subtract fixed-size chunks of memory — one per thread — to determine each new stack’s base address. In the code, we could create an array to store the stack pointer values, where each entry is calculated as:
PSP_base[i] = MSP_init_val - (i + 1) * STACK_SIZE;
This ensures each stack starts at a unique, non-overlapping memory location determined at compile time.

